{"problem": "fixed_windows\n\nReturn a sliding window of width *n* over the given iterable.\n\n    >>> all_windows = fixed_windows([1, 2, 3, 4, 5], 3)\n    >>> list(all_windows)\n    [(1, 2, 3), (2, 3, 4), (3, 4, 5)]\n\nWhen the window is larger than the iterable, *fillvalue* is used in place\nof missing values:\n\n    >>> list(fixed_windows([1, 2, 3], 4))\n    [(1, 2, 3, None)]\n\nEach window will advance in increments of *step*:\n\n    >>> list(fixed_windows([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], 3, fillvalue='!', step=2))\n    [(1, 2, 3), (3, 4, 5), (5, 6, '!')]\n\nTo slide into the iterable's items, use :func:`chain` to add filler items\nto the left:\n\n    >>> iterable = [1, 2, 3, 4]\n    >>> n = 3\n    >>> padding = [None] * (n - 1)\n    >>> list(fixed_windows(chain(padding, iterable), 3))\n    [(None, None, 1), (None, 1, 2), (1, 2, 3), (2, 3, 4)]", "resolution": "def fixed_windows(seq, n, fillvalue=None, step=1):\n    \"\"\"Return a sliding window of width *n* over the given iterable.\n\n        >>> all_windows = fixed_windows([1, 2, 3, 4, 5], 3)\n        >>> list(all_windows)\n        [(1, 2, 3), (2, 3, 4), (3, 4, 5)]\n\n    When the window is larger than the iterable, *fillvalue* is used in place\n    of missing values:\n\n        >>> list(fixed_windows([1, 2, 3], 4))\n        [(1, 2, 3, None)]\n\n    Each window will advance in increments of *step*:\n\n        >>> list(fixed_windows([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], 3, fillvalue='!', step=2))\n        [(1, 2, 3), (3, 4, 5), (5, 6, '!')]\n\n    To slide into the iterable's items, use :func:`chain` to add filler items\n    to the left:\n\n        >>> iterable = [1, 2, 3, 4]\n        >>> n = 3\n        >>> padding = [None] * (n - 1)\n        >>> list(fixed_windows(chain(padding, iterable), 3))\n        [(None, None, 1), (None, 1, 2), (1, 2, 3), (2, 3, 4)]\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError('n must be >= 0')\n    if n == 0:\n        yield ()\n        return\n    if step < 1:\n        raise ValueError('step must be >= 1')\n\n    iterator = iter(seq)\n\n    # Generate head window\n    window = deque(islice(iterator, n), maxlen=n)\n\n    # Deal with the head window not being full\n    if not window:\n        return\n    if len(window) < n:\n        yield tuple(window) + ((fillvalue,) * (n - len(window)))\n        return\n    yield tuple(window)\n\n    # Create the filler for the next windows. The padding ensures\n    # we have just enough elements to fill the final window.\n    padding = (fillvalue,) * (n - 1 if step >= n else step - 1)\n    filler = map(window.append, chain(iterator, padding))\n\n    # Generate the rest of the windows\n    for _ in islice(filler, step - 1, None, step):\n        yield tuple(window)\n", "text": "fixed_windows"}